// Module `simd` (SEM-11). Vectors are `Simd[T, n]`, n × size(T) of 16 or 32 bytes.
// Each operation is typed by its own rule at the call, as `int.widen` is (SEM-1), so
// none has a generic signature here; the declarations land with their checker rows.
//
// wrapping_add(a: V, b: V) -> V        every lane by int.wrapping_add
// wrapping_sub(a: V, b: V) -> V        every lane by int.wrapping_sub
// saturating_add(a: V, b: V) -> V      every lane by int.saturating_add
// saturating_sub(a: V, b: V) -> V      every lane by int.saturating_sub
// eq(a: V, b: V) -> V                  mask: all ones where equal, else 0
// lt(a: V, b: V) -> V                  mask: all ones where a < b as T, else 0
// splat(x: T) -> V                     x in every lane; V from the expected type
// from(a: Inline[T, n]) -> Simd[T, n]  lane i from element i
// swizzle(t: Simd[T, m], i: Simd[u8, n]) -> Simd[T, n]
//                                      T is u8 or i8, m and n are 16 or 32;
//                                      lane k is t[i[k]] when i[k] < m, else 0
// cast(v: V) -> W                      W from the expected type, same size;
//                                      lanes from byte 0, each little-endian
// any(v: V) -> bool                    some lane is not 0
// bitmask(v: V) -> u64                 bit k is the top bit of lane k
//
// In `list`, with V = Simd[u8, n]:
// lanes(b: Bytes, at: u64) -> V        n from the expected type; Bounds unless at + n ≤ len
// put_lanes(mut b: Bytes, v: V, k: u64) -> Result[(), Capacity]
//                                      appends lanes 0 to k − 1; Bounds when k > n;
//                                      grows with needed = len + k (MEM-24)
